  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a user who picks a theme, I want list rows, separators, selection and the native title text to follow the theme too, so that strong themes (Rétro 5250, the OG table look) look whole instead of showing system grey rows on a themed background. Follow-up of LOT-188 option (a) (operator, 2026-11-12, #729).\n\n### Context\n\nLOT-188 (#729, PR #829) recolours the screen backgrounds, the tint, the prominent buttons, the unread capsule and the reader. By decision (a), native list rows and cards keep the system raised colour, and native text keeps the system label colours (`docs/THEMES.md`, \"What a theme does not change\"). Recolouring them needs a `listRowBackground` on each row of every list, which is why this waits for the refactor of #836: done after it, the change goes in the one shared row and list component, not in each copy.\n\n### Blocked by\n\n- #836\n- #829\n\n### Scope\n\n- The tokens `surfaceRaised`, `separator`, `selection`, `title`, `textPrimary`, `textSecondary` and `sectionHeader` reach every native list (rows, cards, section headers, separators, selection) and the native title tones of #651 and #572, through `ThemeAppearance.themeColor(_:)`. No second colour model (LOT-188 spec).\n- Legacy is unchanged (pixel tests of LOT-188 stay green).\n- Contrast rules of `ThemeDefinitionTests` extended to the new pairs (text on `surfaceRaised`, selection).\n- Needed by LOT-192 (#733, Rétro 5250) and LOT-193 (#734, OG clair/gris).\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Every list of the app, as inventoried by #836, follows the theme's row, separator, selection and text tokens. Legacy is pixel-identical.\n- [ ] A test per shared component pins the themed colours. Each test is shown to fail without the change.\n- [ ] Mac check: a strong theme on the lists, the reader, Settings and an iPad split view, in light, dark and Dynamic Type XL.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
